 "title": "Chemostat and Organism Interactions",
 "summary": "This cluster revolves around chemostats, a method or tool used to grow cells in a controlled environment. Organisms such as CoSMO, A-L+, and L-A+ interact with chemostats, with CoSMO being consumed by hypoxanthine and A-L+ having aneuploidy linked to the WY2447 gene or protein. L-A+ is grown in chemostats and has a death rate. Other organisms, such as WY1335 and WY1604, are also present, with WY1604 having a genotype linked to lys−orgS−. The cluster also includes various chemicals, such as lysine, adenine, and hypoxanthine, which are consumed or released by the organisms.",
